In December 2006, we entered into a joint venture agreement with Thonburi Automotive Assembly Plant Co. Ltd. (the 'Thonburi Group') to manufacture pickup trucks in Thailand. As of March 31, 2021, we own 97.21% of the joint venture, while the Thonburi Group owns the remaining 2.79%. The joint venture, which began vehicle production in March 2008, enabled us to access the Thailand market, which is a major market for pickup trucks, as well as other potential markets in the ASEAN region. On July 31, 2018, the Company decided to cease its current manufacturing operations of Tata Motors Thailand Ltd and shall continue to address the Thailand market with a revamped product portfolio, suitable to local market needs, delivered through a CBU distribution model.

